[gd_scene load_steps=47 format=3]

; Tri-axle box / curtainside semi-trailer. Hand-built low-poly (Kenney ships no trailers at all),
; flat boxes and 10-segment cylinders to match the kit's flat-shaded look.
;
; AUTHORED WITH THE ORIGIN AT THE KINGPIN, ground at y = -1.05 — the family convention, measured
; off the tractor unit's fifth-wheel plate. See flatbed.tscn's header for why: the coupling datum
; is the origin, so Articulation.coupled_pose is one transform multiply and the joint sits exactly
; on this node.
;
; THE HEAVIEST TRAILER AND NOTHING ELSE — no PTO, no valve, no interlock, no load model. That is
; the phase's lesson rather than an unfinished trailer, and box.gd states it in full.
;
; MEASURED against the tractor unit, never guessed: 1.92 wide (the truck family's width), a 6.50 m
; body on the family's 5.40 m frame behind the same 1.35 m gooseneck, roof at y 1.48 = 2.53 m above
; the road. The cab's roof is 2.12, so the box stands taller than the unit pulling it, which is
; what makes an artic read as an artic from behind.
;
; IT IS A GOOSENECK, and that is structural: NOTHING may hang below the coupling plane (y = 0) over
; the tractor. So the FLOOR IS IN TWO PANELS — the neck-top panel at y 0.25 forward of z 1.05 and
; the deck panel at y -0.16 behind it — and the side walls step with them. Authored as one flat
; floor the panel ran straight through the tractor's fifth wheel and frame rails.
;
; Swing clearance is geometry, not taste: the frontmost parts are the neck and the side walls above
; it, 0.33 m ahead of the kingpin at 0.96 half-width, so they swing on sqrt(0.96^2 + 0.33^2) =
; 1.02 m — inside the 1.15 m from the kingpin to the cab's rear face. test_trailer sweeps every
; part of every trailer for this rather than trusting a node name.
;
; The curtain side is authored as its steel: top rail, bottom rave and five tensioning straps a
; side. A curtainsider's body IS the same trailer as a box van with a sheet where the panel is,
; which is the other half of why this trailer adds nothing but mass.
;
; Undriven and unsteered: the axles only ever brake. Suspension/mass/grip live in box_spec.tres.

